+rudrama-devi | 1260 | Telangana | women, power | deccan | Rudrama Devi | Rudrama Devi becomes co-ruler | Rudrama Devi was a ruling queen of the Kakatiya dynasty, who governed substantial parts of today's Telangana and Andhra Pradesh. Her father Ganapati, who had no son, appointed her as his co-regent around 1260. | Around 1260 the Kakatiya king had no son, so he made his daughter Rudrama Devi ruler alongside him. She went on to rule a large kingdom.
