+jahanara | 1631 | India | women, power | all | Jahanara Begum | Jahanara, first lady of the empire | Jahanara Begum was the eldest surviving child of the Mughal emperor Shah Jahan and Mumtaz Mahal. After her mother's death in 1631, the 17-year-old Jahanara was entrusted with the royal seal and given the title Padshah Begum. | When the empress Mumtaz Mahal died in 1631, her 17-year-old daughter Jahanara was put in charge of the royal seal of the Mughal Empire.
